# .agent/Dockerfile — OPTIONAL overlay for this project's root/system deps.
#
# `agent init` does NOT write this file; copy it to `.agent/Dockerfile` and
# uncomment to use it. When present, the CLI builds it FROM the versioned base
# image and runs the result; when absent, the base image is used directly.
#
# What goes here vs .agent/init.sh:
#   • Overlay (this file): root/system deps — `apt-get install`, /usr/local
#     binaries, browser libraries. Built BEFORE launch, as root.
#   • init.sh: everything user-space and repo-dependent (`npm ci`, `uv sync`),
#     run as the non-root `node` user after the clone.
#
# The CLI injects the base image tag as the BASE build-arg, so there is no
# version literal to let drift. The build context is `.agent/` and the repo
# clone does NOT exist at build time — do not reference repo files here.

# ARG BASE
# FROM ${BASE}
#
# USER root
# RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
#         some-system-package \
#     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
# USER node
